# Gapless fast path: THE ARM PATCH. Deliberately NOT in the default
# manifest. Stacks on top of 0020-0025. Applying it is the decision to
# enable decoder-image retention on hardware; the Phase D observation
# named in gapless_patch.md (resident decoder accepting the stock 0x65
# open exchange after end-of-stream) must be on record first.
name: gapless-6-arm
kind: module
module: 0
region: code
address: 0x03051674
gate: build refuses unless the 2 bytes at the target equal `expect`
  (the gate cave as installed by 0022); the finished image must also
  pass firmware_patch.validate()
rationale: One branch inside the gate cave at 0x03051664 (0022). As
  shipped by 0022 the instruction at cave+0x10 is an unconditional
  branch to the stock path (ffe7), so the same-module comparison the
  cave performs is ignored and every decoder load runs the stock
  reset-and-start body. This patch replaces those 2 bytes with
  `beq` to the cave's skip block (02d0): when the retained module word
  (masked) equals the requested decoder module, the gate records
  module|0x80 and returns to the codec case without running the
  reset-and-start body -- no image re-copy, no core-1 reset, no
  parameter-page re-copy, no ready poll -- and the delay cut (0023)
  becomes live for same-rate transitions. Nothing else changes.
expect: ffe7
replace: 02d0
